NOTICE — external data sources and reused components
home-energy-twin
===============================================================================

Purpose
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This file lists every external data source and reused component named in the
repository docs, together with the terms stated for it in those docs and the
attribution string that must be carried by any output derived from it.

Authority for every statement below is in-repo only:
  docs/RUBBER-DUCK-REVIEW.md  RD-2 (privacy posture), RD-3 (safety posture),
                              RD-11 (data-licensing traps / NOTICE requirement)
  docs/PLAN.md                §1 architecture, §3 adapter interfaces,
                              §4 build-vs-reuse table, §6 privacy & security posture
  specs/SPEC.md               LAW-6 (no telemetry by default), LAW-7 (read-only v1),
                              LAW-8 (no safety claims), LAW-12 (provenance everywhere)

Where the repo docs do not state the terms or the exact attribution wording for
a source, this file says so explicitly rather than inventing it:

    "terms not stated in repo docs — verify before use"

Adding a data source to the project requires adding its entry here (RD-11).

Rule (RD-11, LAW-12): the Open-Meteo server code is never embedded; Open-Meteo
is called through its hosted API only. Any output that carries Open-Meteo or
other CC BY 4.0 data must carry that source's attribution string.

