-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Standing obligations that follow from the entries above
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * LAW-6  No telemetry by default: no network call for analytics, crash
           reporting or usage statistics. External calls happen only to
           data/weather/device endpoints the user configured, and are
           enumerable in config.
  * LAW-7  v1 is read-only: no code path actuates HVAC or any device.
  * LAW-8  No safety claims in any shipped output.
  * LAW-12 Provenance everywhere: every series and cost figure carries source
           + retrieved/as-of metadata and, where the source's terms require it,
           the attribution string above. A number without provenance does not
           reach a report.
  * RD-2   Local-first reference deployment; no project-operated cloud; no
           telemetry by default; encryption at rest for stored series; secrets
           in the OS/secret store; retention + downsampling controls; one-action
           house deletion; a threat-model document is required before Phase 2.
  * RD-3   v1 is read-only/advisory, full stop; alert copy is constrained; no
           safety-device claims anywhere; any future control needs a separate
           owner-approved safety spec.
  * RD-11  This NOTICE is the registry: adding a source requires adding its
           entry.

See docs/PRIVACY_AND_SAFETY.md for the posture statements these obligations
back up.
